const originalGetComputedStyle = window.getComputedStyle;
afterEach restore via vi.restoreAllMocks? config restoreMocks true after each, but manually append cleanup.
```
`vi.spyOn(window, "getComputedStyle").mockReturnValue(...)`; restoreMocks handles. Need no afterEach.
`expect(window.scrollTo).toHaveBeenCalledWith({top:104, behavior:"smooth"})`.
Set section top 200, header 80 => 200-96=104.
- Hash update: spy history.pushState. But jsdom history.pushState is function. `vi.spyOn(window.history, "pushState")`.
- reduced motion: spy matchMedia. create object maybe `as MediaQueryList`. Need `vi.spyOn(window, "matchMedia").mockImplementation((query) => ({...}))`; return object.
- `window.scrollTo` is vi.fn from setup. clearMocks clears each test.
- useScrollSpy test: save original IO. In test, class:
```
let notify: IntersectionObserverCallback | undefined;
const observe = vi.fn();
const disconnect = vi.fn();
class FakeIO {
 root=null; rootMargin=""; thresholds=[];
 constructor(cb){notify=cb}
 observe=observe; unobserve=vi.fn(); disconnect=disconnect; takeRecords=()=>[];
}
globalThis.IntersectionObserver = FakeIO as unknown as typeof IntersectionObserver;
const {result} = renderHook(()=>useScrollSpy(["home","activities","services"]));
expect(result.current).toBe("home");
act(()=>notify!(... , {} as IntersectionObserver));
expect(result.current).toBe("services");
```
Need when ids "home","activities","services" default home. Callback sets visible services. sectionIds.find visible -> services. Good.
Then clear services, callback with no intersect -> no next, state stays services. Not important.
Restore IO after. Use afterEach:
```
const originalIO = globalThis.IntersectionObserver;
afterEach(() => { globalThis.IntersectionObserver = originalIO; });
```
But test setup's Mock restored. Good.
