Only hover lifts and arrow shift. Add global reduced-motion `translate: none !important;` to suppress. Or replace `motion-reduce:transform-none` with `motion-reduce:translate-none` if exists. I'm not sure `translate-none` utility exists in Tailwind 4. It might: tailwind has `translate-none` for `translate: none`. Could test build. Simpler global:
```
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    ...
    translate: none !important;
  }
}
```
But `translate` property applies only to transformable elements; none resets. Good. Does it override hover? `!important` yes.
This will also suppress any translate used for positioning; none currently. Good.

Also current motion script no-preference hover didn't apply, but reduce didΓÇöweird ordering due emulation/navigation and mouse state. Regardless, reduce showed translate nonzero, proving bug. After fix should none.

Add `translate: none !important;` in media query. Also perhaps `scale: none !important;`? No hover scale used. Not necessary.

Then rebuild and rerun motion. Also this is a functional fix from T110. Do it.

